> Quartz is one of the most common and varied[ minerals] on earth, and its abundant colors produce many gemstone types. Amethyst and Citrine are the most popular and valuable gem varieties of[ Quartz], but other forms also make important gemstones.[ Chal]cedony describes any form of[ Quartz] that is micro[crystall]ine, in[ compact] form without any[ visible crystals].[ Chal]cedony also has[ several] varieties used as[ gemstones], most notably[ Ag]ate,[ Carn]elian, Tiger's Eye, and Chrysoprase.
